{
 "name": "megarachne",
 "description": "Megarachne servinei as it really was: a short, broad freshwater sea scorpion (eurypterid), top view, head right. Wide, almost circular head shield with two small dark eyes near the front, short broad body of four wide segments ending stubby (no tail spike), front limbs carrying comb-like raking blades held forward and out, two pairs of sturdy walking legs. Dull mud brown #6b5235 with a darker back. Not jaekelopterus: no long body, no pincers, no paddles. Anchor centre, ~510x380 (x -268..242, y -192..192).",
